# Shell scripts are LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# A CRLF shebang is not a shebang. The interpreter reads `#!/bin/bash\r`, looks
# for a program called `bash\r`, and reports `/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter` or
# `\r: command not found` — neither of which names the file or the real cause.
# This repository is developed on Windows, so without the rule at the root a new
# script in a new directory rediscovers the problem.
*.sh text eol=lf
